.TH XVFB-RUN 1 "2026-09-30" "1g4 Linux"
.SH NAME
xvfb-run \- run a command in a private virtual X display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xvfb-run
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xvfb-run
creates an X authority cookie, starts Xvfb, waits for it to accept connections,
and runs the command with DISPLAY and XAUTHORITY set.
After the command exits, the wrapper stops Xvfb and removes its cookie and
temporary directory.
TCP listening is disabled by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -a ", " --auto-servernum
Find an available display starting at the requested server number.
Retry startup at most ten times.
.TP
.BR -n " NUM, " --server-num=NUM
Use display NUM, a nonnegative integer. The default is 99.
.TP
.BR -e " FILE, " --error-file=FILE
Append Xvfb and xauth diagnostics to FILE. The default is /dev/null.
/dev/stdout and /dev/stderr duplicate the corresponding open descriptor.
.TP
.BR -f " FILE, " --auth-file=FILE
Use FILE for the authority cookie instead of a private temporary file.
The wrapper removes its display's cookie on exit but does not delete FILE.
.TP
.BR -s " ARGS, " --server-args=ARGS
Pass whitespace-separated arguments to Xvfb.
Shell quoting inside ARGS is not interpreted and pathname patterns are not
expanded. The default is "-screen 0 1280x1024x24".
.TP
.BR -l ", " --listen-tcp
Enable TCP listening.
.TP
.BR -p " PROTO, " --xauth-protocol=PROTO
Select the xauth protocol. The default is xauth's default protocol.
.TP
.BR -w " SECONDS, " --wait=SECONDS
Accepted for compatibility and ignored. Startup uses Xvfb's readiness signal.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Display help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Parent directory for the private temporary authority file. Defaults to /tmp.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command's exit status is returned.
Wrapper failures return 1 for Xvfb startup, 2 for a missing command or invalid
display number, 3 for a missing runtime tool, 5 for a temporary-directory
cleanup failure after a successful command, and 6 for invalid options.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B xvfb-run -a -e /dev/stderr gtk-test
.SH AUTHORS
Branden Robinson and Jeff Licquia; maintained locally in the bp repository
for 1g4 Linux.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Xvfb (1),
.BR xauth (1)
